  "notes": "<p>This show was Phish's 95th performance at Madison Square Garden, included several 1995-related references (a setlist composed of songs from the band's 1995 era, Trey wearing a Jah Volunteer shirt, a chess board, and a mini drum kit) and featured multiple bustouts: Ha Ha Ha (last played <a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-august-27-2021-gorge-amphitheatre-george-wa-usa.html\">August 27, 2021</a>, or 231 shows), Drowned (last played <a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-october-15-2023-united-center-chicago-il-usa.html\">October 15, 2023</a>, or 113 shows), and Johnny B. Goode (last played August 8, 1998, or 927 shows. Wilson was preceded by Page checkmating the audience. Timber (Jerry the Mule), Halley's Comet, Prince Caspian, Drowned, and It's Ice featured Trey on a mini drum kit. Trey teased Rainy Day Woman #12 &amp; 35 in Timber (Jerry the Mule), San-Ho-Zay in Halley's Comet, Tequila and Cissy Strut in Drowned, and Johnny B. Goode in Loving Cup.</p>",
